- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`

**How to implement.** The object stage's results are read off each linear solve it made (step 390): its design over the matrix's sixteen elements, each run's rows within it, and for a series the product check against the cascade of its objects' own solves (001 §L 'the product check for series objects (M_comb against M_LR · M_QZ)'; the S11.4 brief 'REUSE MuellerReconstruction.cascadeProduct and the RMSE ratio S10.3 computes'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4. In `StudyEngine.fs`, after `nonlinearProblemsWith` (step 399): (1) `ObjectRunSystem = { run : ExperimentName; system : LeastSquaresSystem }` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:LeastSquaresSystem`), one run's projected rows, and `ObjectGroupSystem = { items : ItemId list; runs : ObjectRunSystem list }` with `member this.system : LeastSquaresSystem`, `LeastSquaresSystem.concat` of its runs' systems in order (step 388). (2) `type StagedStudy with member this.objectSystemsWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) (data : StudyData) : Result<ObjectGroupSystem list, StudyFitError>`: the projection and grouping of `reconstructLinear` (step 390) MOVED, each run's system `LeastSquaresSystem.ofProjections` of its own capture rows' projections (step 388), the groups in the order of their first run, the errors as there. `reconstructLinear` becomes `objectSystemsWith` followed, for each group, by `reconstruct solver group.system` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:reconstruct`) and what it did with each solve. The runs' rows concatenated in run order are the system it solved, row for row, so every number it answers is unchanged. (3) `type ProductCheckData with member this.storedFor (items : ItemId list) : SeriesProductCheck` (step 352): its cascade's `rowMajorValues` (step 390), its difference and its two RMSEs; and `type SeriesProductCheck with member this.rmseRatio : ProductRmseRatio`, `ProductRmseRatio.between this.productRmse this.fitRmse` (step 352), the one place the stored check's ratio is formed. (4) `type StagedStudy with member this.objectProblemsWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) (data : StudyData) (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) : Result<EngineProblems, StudyFitError>`, for a solution `reconstructLinear` answered. Over the context with `kit.items` replaced by `this.items` and its layout (step 372), `objectSystemsWith`, then each group's `reconstruct solver group.system` (an error `ObjectSolveFitErr` as in step 390) gives one `FittedProblem` (step 397): `ObjectSolveProblem group.items`; sixteen coordinates in the solve's own order, k = 4c + r for the element (r, c) (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:vecColumnMajor`), each, for a group of one item, `EntryCoordinate [ <the layout entry of that item's m<r><c>, with its ItemOwner> ]` and, for a series, `ElementCoordinate (MuellerRowIndex r, MuellerColumnIndex c)`; the residual s ↦ `ResidualVector` of `group.system.residualsAt` s (step 394); a `search` starting at the solved matrix's `vecColumnMajor`, within each entry's unknown bounds for one item and unbounded (`infinity`, `OptimizationInterface.fs:ParameterBounds`) for a series; centre zero and unit one. `runResiduals` hold, run by run in study order, each run's own `system.residualsAt` its group's solution, with their root mean square. `productChecks` hold, for each group of two or more items, in order, whose every item has a group of its own, `productCheckOf later first series group.system` (step 352) stored for `group.items`: `first` the first item's own matrix, `later` the cascade of the others' own matrices in light order (for [i₁; i₂; …; iₖ], `cascadeProduct` of each next one onto the product so far, so that `productCheckOf`'s `cascadeProduct later first` is Mₖ ⋯ M₂ · M₁, for [QZ; LR] exactly M_LR · M_QZ, `MuellerReconstruction.fs:cascadeProduct`), and `series` the group's own solve. No other member is added. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`, over step 390's fixture: `an object solve's problem is its design over the matrix's elements, each coordinate an entry of the object`: QZ's problem is `ObjectSolveProblem [ QZ ]`, its coordinate 4c + r QZ's `m<r><c>` entry, its start equal to QZ's fitted entries in that order exactly, and its quality of rank 16 with a condition within 1e-6 relative of `(ResidualJacobian <its design rows>).conditionNumber`; with every row's `avgTotal` moved by 0.01 · (−1)ⁱ, each of its sixteen `sigmaAt` is `Some` and above zero, and the one of `m00` is √(χ² / (m − 16) · (AᵀA)⁻¹₀₀) within 1e-6 relative, computed in the test through `RealMatrix`; `each run of an object stage has its own rows' residual at its object's solve`: each Science run's `RunResidual` holds its own rows' A · x − b at QZ's solve, with their root mean square, run by run; `a series is checked against the cascade of its objects' own solves`: with the series runs of QZ then LR added (step 390), one `SeriesProductCheck` for [QZ; LR] whose cascade is `cascadeProduct` of LR's and QZ's own solved matrices element by element within 1e-12, whose difference's `maxAbs` is below 1e-9 and whose `fitRmse` is the series' `ObjectMatrixFit` RMSE, and the series' problem has sixteen `ElementCoordinate`s. Step 390's facts over `reconstructLinear` run unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the object problems land, `StagedStudy.objectProblemsWith` MUST answer each object solve's design over its sixteen elements, each run's own residual and each series' product check against the cascade of its objects' own solves, and `reconstructLinear` MUST answer what it answered before; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an object solve's problem is its design over the matrix's elements, each coordinate an entry of the object`, `each run of an object stage has its own rows' residual at its object's solve` and `a series is checked against the cascade of its objects' own solves`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.
